---
import RobotConversation from './RobotConversation.astro';
---
<RobotConversation>
  <Fragment slot="consent">
    <details data-ai-consent>
      <summary>Optional local AI</summary>
      <p>Download about 204 MB plus runtime files to draft answers on your device. Requires a compatible GPU. Answers may be withheld when they cannot be grounded in the sources.</p>
      <p>Questions go to this site's public resume service. Model hosts receive download requests. Files may stay in your browser cache.</p>
      <button type="button" data-enable>Download and enable AI</button>
    </details>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="about">
  <details class="robot-about">
    <summary>Sources, privacy, and model</summary>
    <p>
      Evidence comes from Tim's curated, public resume records and may
      include self-reported or historical claims. A search match does not
      confirm a question's premise. Expand each source to read its full details
      and qualifications. Source identifiers are shown as text; external
      links come only from those records.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI is optional and can make factual mistakes. It uses a bounded selection
      of complete retrieved records with their qualifications. Conversation
      stays in page memory, up to 12 questions per session. Clear starts a new
      session. Closing this dialog stops requests and unloads local inference.
      Downloaded model files may remain in your browser cache.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI inference runs on your device, never on a server. Runtime: <a
        href="https://github.com/mlc-ai/web-llm"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">WebLLM</a
      >. Model: <a
        href="https://huggingface.co/mlc-ai/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-q4f16_1-MLC"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">MLC SmolLM2 360M</a
      >, using f16 or f32 according to GPU support. WebLLM and the <a
        href="https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">upstream SmolLM2 model</a
      > use Apache 2.0. See publisher pages for license and provenance.
    </p>
    <a href="/resume/mcp">Resume MCP connection guide</a>
  </details>
  </Fragment>
</RobotConversation>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/robot/host';
</script>
